infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two ways Postgres runs the collapse
  desc Planner picks HashAggregate while the hash table fits work_mem; else sort-based GroupAggregate
  compares
    - label HashAggregate
      children
        - label Unsorted input — builds a hash table
          desc One entry per group, keyed by user_id
        - label Every distinct key in memory at once
          desc ~2M groups × ~50–100 B of state
        - label Spills when it exceeds work_mem
          desc On the 4 MB default: ~320 MB to a temp file, 4–6s
    - label GroupAggregate
      children
        - label Needs input pre-sorted by key
          desc A preceding Sort or an ordered index scan
        - label Streams one bucket at a time
          desc Emits then discards each → near-constant memory
        - label Pays the sort up front
          desc No hash-table spill, but the sort isn't free
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
